1. Definitions
   "Software" means the original work provided by Lumyrix, in source or
   binary form.
   "Fork" means a modified version of the Software that contains changes
   beyond mere bug fixes, as described below.
   "Distribute" means making the Software or a Fork available to others,
   whether in source or binary form, including but not limited to posting on
   public repositories, mod platforms, or file hosting services.

2. Forking and Modifications
   a. Anyone may create a Fork of the Software for private or public use.
   b. A Fork must include significant modifications, such as the addition,
      removal, or alteration of features. A modification that only corrects
      errors (bug fixes) is not considered a significant modification.
      You may not distribute a Fork that consists solely of bug fixes without
      the prior written approval of the Original Author. If you discover a
      bug, you are strongly encouraged to report it to the Original Author
      so it may be addressed in the original Software.
   c. A Fork may add, remove, or modify any features without restriction, as
      long as all other conditions are met.

3. Redistribution
   a. You may NOT distribute the original, unmodified Software in any form.
      This includes uploading the exact Software binary or source code to
      any website, repository, or mod platform (including Modrinth,
      CurseForge, GitHub, etc.).
   b. You may distribute a Fork that complies with this License on any
      platform, including Modrinth and CurseForge, provided the Fork is
      clearly distinct from the original Software and follows all naming
      and branding rules.

4. Source Code and License of Forks
   a. If you distribute a Fork in binary form, you must make the complete
      corresponding source code publicly available under the terms of this
      License. The source code must be provided in a readily accessible
      manner (for example, a public repository) or made available on request.
   b. Private Forks that are never distributed do not require source code
      publication.
   c. Any distributed Fork must be licensed in its entirety under this
      License (the Lumyrix Source License). You may not impose any additional
      restrictions on the recipients' exercise of the rights granted herein.
      This ensures all modifications remain open under the same terms.

5. Attribution and Authorship
   a. You are not required to include the original copyright notice or the
      name "Lumyrix" in your Fork.
   b. You may add your own name and copyright notice to a Fork. You may
      also include a statement such as "Based on Lumyrix" or similar, as
      long as it does not misrepresent the origin of the code.
   c. You must NOT claim or imply that you are the original author of the
      unmodified Software. Any suggestion that you created the original work
      is strictly prohibited.

6. Naming and Branding
   a. You may not use the original name of the Software for any Fork.
      A Fork must be distributed under a new, distinct name.
   b. You may not reuse, reproduce, or distribute the logos, icons, or other
      distinctive visual assets that are part of the original Software.
   c. Even if a Fork is significantly different, the name must be changed;
      this requirement applies to all Forks without exception.

